---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {projects} from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="Start contributing" description="Get started contributing to AppKade-maintained open-source projects and earn verifiable credit."><div class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Every contribution counts</p><h1>Start contributing</h1><p class="lede">No AppKade account, application form or approval queue. Collaboration happens where the code lives: GitHub.</p></div><section class="section"><div class="grid"><article class="card"><p class="tagline">Step 01</p><h3>Choose a project</h3><p>Explore published projects. Look for open issues that match your interests.</p><a href="/projects/">Browse projects →</a></article><article class="card"><p class="tagline">Step 02</p><h3>Open a pull request</h3><p>Follow each repository's guidelines and discuss changes through code review.</p><a href="https://github.com/AppKade">Visit organization ↗</a></article><article class="card"><p class="tagline">Step 03</p><h3>See verified recognition</h3><p>After an eligible PR is merged, your GitHub-linked contribution becomes visible in the next sync.</p><a href="/docs/contributing/">Scoring rules →</a></article></div></section><section class="section"><h2>Where to begin</h2><div class="stack">{projects.map(p=><article class="card"><h3><a href={`/projects/${p.slug}/`}>{p.name}</a></h3><p>{p.description}</p><a class="text-link" href={`https://github.com/${p.repo}/issues`}>See open issues ↗</a></article>)}</div></section><section class="section card"><h2>Keep it useful</h2><p class="muted">Spam pull requests and artificially split changes won't earn recognition. Maintainers review quality and classification. All points must link back to an actual merged PR.</p><a href="https://github.com/AppKade/open/issues">Questions or suggestions? Open an issue ↗</a></section></Base>
